        "class_notes": [
          "Upon satisfactorily completing Clusters M27A, M27B, and M27CW, students receive credit for the following requirements: one Literary and Cultural Analysis GE, one Historical Analysis GE, two Social Analysis GEs.",
          "Upon satisfactorily completing Clusters M27A, M27B, and M27CW students will fulfill the Writing II requirement.",
          "Students must receive a grade of D- or better each quarter to receive general education credit and continue in the course.",
          "To receive credit for Writing II, students must satisfy Writing I by the end of the year, successfully complete fall and winter quarters, and earn a grade of C or better in spring quarter.",
          "For a complete summary of clusters credits, see https://www.uei.ucla.edu/academic-programs/ucla-cluster-program/benefits ."
        ],
        "requisites": [],
        "grading": "Letter Grade or Passed/ Not Passed",
        "impacted": "No",
        "level": "Lower Division",
        "course_description": "(Same as Clusters M27A.) Lecture, three hours; discussion, two hours. Course M27A is enforced requisite to M27B, which is enforced requisite to M27CW. Introduction to Islam, immensely diverse global tradition which is second largest religion. Study of Islam and Muslims within framework of study of global religious traditions and emphasis on profound diversity of localized belief and practice found across world. Examination of Islam's evolution across 15 centuries, from late antiquity--when it emerged as localized religion in Central Arabia--to modern era where it is practice from U.S. to Indonesia. Concentration on broad analytical categories in study of religion such as text, culture, history, and prophecy. Students transition to more complex analyses through chronological overview of Islamic history. Study also of case studies of Muslim global networks in arenas such as art, music, literature, and political thought. P/NP or letter grading.",
