        "requisites": [],
        "grading": "Letter Grade or Passed/ Not Passed",
        "impacted": "No",
        "level": "Lower Division",
        "course_description": "Lecture, three hours; discussion, one hour. Assumptions about work, including why some work is favored, whether those with good jobs really are better people than those without, and how this understanding of work and value came to be common sense. Unpacking of these and other assumptions about work, value, and power, with focus on low-wage workers, their communities, and their place in contemporary society. P/NP or letter grading.",
