        "course_description": "(Same as Psychology M116A.) Lecture, one hour; laboratory, three hours. Requisites: courses M101A and M101B (M101B may be taken concurrently), or Psychology 10, 100A, 100B, and 115. Not open for credit to students with credit for Psychology 116B. Designed for Psychobiology, Psychology, and Neuroscience majors. Laboratory experience with various topics in behavioral neuroscience. Hands-on experience with important methodology and experimental approaches in neuroscience. P/NP or letter grading.",
